TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The report states that oceans have become 30 percent more acidic since the industrial revolution. This is misleading: ocean acidity has increased by about 30%, corresponding to a decrease in pH of roughly 0.1, not a 30% change in acidity expressed as pH."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The proposed near-real-time monitoring and reef-colour detection are not translated into a defined sensor payload, spatial or temporal resolution, coverage, or data-delivery requirements."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"The plan mentions selecting orbit and altitude but gives no preliminary orbit, launch, coverage, or access analysis; thus the required space-segment application of course material remains prospective."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"No technical calculations or STK outputs are included, despite the schedule listing STK simulations; reported tutorial completion alone does not substantiate preliminary design progress."}],"overall":"A clear Australian mission rationale, substantial timetable, and useful source list are provided. However, mission requirements remain vague and the space-segment design and technical progress are largely future work. Strengthen measurable user-driven requirements and include preliminary orbit or coverage analysis and simulation evidence.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The rationale and Australian benefit are clear, and marine and conservation scientists are identified as users. The proposed monitoring capability is relevant, but the mission lacks specific objectives, measurable requirements, and detail on how its instruments or data would meet user needs.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"This tool could be applied to a new satellite over the Great Barrier Reef."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":21.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A detailed week-by-week Gantt chart and descriptions cover research, launch, orbit, ground control, communications, simulations, and finalisation. Multiple information sources are listed. The plan has limited contingencies and does not explain dependencies or why the schedule is optimised for this mission, so it is at the lower end of Accomplished.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"The goal is to brainstorm and research as many possible strategies for the satellite’s launch/orbit"},{"where":"Useful Links","quote":"https://coralreefwatch.noaa.gov/satellite/publications/nim_skirving_reef_vulnerability.pdf"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Some research and software familiarisation are reported, but no preliminary calculations, orbit selection, design parameters, or simulation results are presented. This demonstrates minor progress rather than a useful preliminary technical result.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner’s monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity, and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":12.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report has a logical structure, headings, a labelled and readable Gantt chart, and sources. Presentation is generally understandable but has some awkward phrasing, and references are primarily bare URLs with limited formal citation detail. It is competent but not fully professional.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue. Deadlines are indicated by red lines."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"¹ https://www.noaa.gov/education/resource-collections/ocean-coasts/ocean-acidification"}]}]}
